<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Refusal by Prompt</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ D.1 Refusal by Sociodemographic ‣ Appendix D Results ‣ No for Some, Yes for Others:Persona Prompts and Other Sources of False Refusal in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, <a href="#A4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ D.1 Refusal by Sociodemographic ‣ Appendix D Results ‣ No for Some, Yes for Others:Persona Prompts and Other Sources of False Refusal in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> show the variation of false refusals across models and prompt strictness response lev-
els (unforced-response, semi-forced response and
forced-response) for the NLI and politeness tasks, respectively. For a detailed discussion on these results, see §<a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Refusal by Prompt ‣ 4 Results ‣ No for Some, Yes for Others:Persona Prompts and Other Sources of False Refusal in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
